args: opentide --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Spec-driven development for agentic detection engineering

␛[1m␛[4mUsage:␛[0m ␛[1mopentide␛[0m [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

␛[1m␛[4mOptions:␛[0m
      ␛[1m--repo␛[0m <REPO>
          Repository root
          
          [env: OPENTIDE_REPO_ROOT]

      ␛[1m--data␛[0m <DATA>
          Data root; only --technique completion reads it
          
          [env: OPENTIDE_DATA_ROOT]

      ␛[1m--debug␛[0m
          Enable debug logging. Also OPENTIDE_DEBUG=1

      ␛[1m--quiet␛[0m
          Print only the outcome line and errors

      ␛[1m--verbose␛[0m
          Also print notes, such as a missing optional field. --json always includes them

      ␛[1m--no-color␛[0m
          Disable colour

      ␛[1m--json␛[0m
          Machine-readable output: one JSON object on stdout

      ␛[1m--proxy␛[0m <PROXY>
          HTTP(S) proxy URL (http://[user:pass@]host:port) for platform and lookup calls. Overrides HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY; hosts in NO_PROXY are still reached directly.
          
          [env: OPENTIDE_PROXY]

  ␛[1m-V␛[0m, ␛[1m--version␛[0m
          Print the installed opentide version and exit

      ␛[1m--install-completion␛[0m
          Install completion; name a shell after it to pick one

      ␛[1m--show-completion␛[0m
          Print the script instead; name a shell after it to pick one

      ␛[1m--help␛[0m
          Print help

␛[1m␛[4mAuthor:␛[0m
  ␛[1mvalidate␛[0m  Validate objects and queries
  ␛[1mquery␛[0m     Run a read-only query on platform tenants and show rows
  ␛[1mlint␛[0m      Check file names and recommended metadata
  ␛[1minfo␛[0m      Show repository and platform information
  ␛[1mnew␛[0m       Scaffold a threat, objective or rule from its template
  ␛[1mgenerate␛[0m  Generate schemas, templates, docs and exports
  ␛[1mrules␛[0m     Detection rule maintenance

␛[1m␛[4mShip:␛[0m
  ␛[1mdeploy␛[0m    Deploy rules to platform tenants
  ␛[1mshare␛[0m     Publish objects to intelligence platforms

␛[1m␛[4mWorkspace:␛[0m
  ␛[1msetup␛[0m     Set up a detection repository and its tooling
  ␛[1mdoctor␛[0m    Check the installation, the workspace and its integrations
  ␛[1mmigrate␛[0m   Rewrite objects for a newer opentide model
  ␛[1mtui␛[0m       Browse the catalogue and its diagnostics in a terminal UI

␛[1m␛[4mAgents and integrations:␛[0m
  ␛[1mexplain␛[0m   Explain a diagnostic code and how to fix it
  ␛[1mcommands␛[0m  List every command and option, for agents
  ␛[1mmcp␛[0m       Run the opentide MCP server for editors and agents
  ␛[1mlsp␛[0m       Serve the language server for editors
  ␛[1mserve␛[0m     Run CLI commands in one warm process, for editors

Examples:
  $ opentide setup
  $ opentide validate
  $ opentide --json validate

